bibliograph-worker (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.1 release: lexicon.community PR #18 edition records.

    - Build published edition records with contributors[].displayName and
      ONIX role codes (normalized; default A01) from the imported PR #18
      defs lexicon, replacing the legacy name/author fields.
    - Republish existing editions through pds_outbox so PDS records match the
      new contributor shape without changing URIs.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.0 release: catalog reliability and curation.

    - Retry provider calls with per-provider circuit breakers, and expose the
      breaker state and ISBNdb daily usage on the metrics listener.
    - Enforce the daily ISBNdb quota before a request is made, and reject
      ISBNdb calls while its breaker is open.
    - Add the authenticated admin API (ADMIN_TOKEN) for provider search,
      publisher search, publisher book preview and bounded bulk import.
    - Keep ISBNdb citation and synopsis text intact while unwrapping.
    - Ship the versioned catalog schema (0001-0003) inside the package.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package. The graphile-worker from packages/worker, with its
    production dependencies deployed beside it:

    - catalog.resolve / catalog.search hydrate the catalog from Google Books,
      ISBNdb and Goodreads;
    - pds-publish drains public.pds_outbox into the publisher PDS with
      com.atproto.repo.applyWrites, choosing create/update from pds_cids and
      recording the returned CID;
    - /etc/bibliograph/worker.env carries the database URL, publisher identity
      and optional provider keys.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
